WHAT IS HERE

`../code/` is a pristine clone of ScholarQABench at

    95e6fc52b0a8a0ce0a74956029991e3bb00c38b9

and `../../setup.sh --check` asserts it stays that way. These three files are
ours: derived from upstream's, changed substantially, and maintained here rather
than in the clone. Upstream never imports them — they are standalone scripts,
invoked by path — so moving them out costs nothing. `run_utils.py` stays beside
them because `citation_correctness_eval.py` imports it as a flat module, the way
it does upstream.

MODIFICATIONS

  - `citation_correctness_eval.py` — roughly twice its upstream length
    (+935/-200). Added: a configurable AutoAIS input-token cap with an
    out-of-memory fallback that retries at successively shorter limits, chunked
    scoring with an optional model reload per chunk (`--autoais_chunk_size`,
    `--autoais_reload_model_per_chunk`), and a per-question results dump. These
    make the full 1451- and 1308-question sets scoreable on one GPU; they do not
    change how a citation is judged.
  - `prometheus_eval.py` (+719/-163) — points at a judge served over an
    OpenAI-compatible endpoint (`--model litellm_openai`, `--litellm_api_base`,
    `--litellm_model`) instead of loading it in-process, and scores one set of
    rubric aspects per invocation (`--aspects`), so the two judges can take
    turns on the same GPUs.
  - `run_utils.py` (+24/-10) — retry with exponential backoff on rate limits,
    plus logging and formatting.

Upstream's `requirements.txt` became `../../envs/sqa-scoring.in`, reduced to
what these two scorers import and resolved for Linux.

WHAT WE DID NOT CHANGE

Everything else in the clone, including `rubrics/prometheus_rubrics_v8.json`,
which is read straight out of it.

Our internal tree also carries changes to the ScholarQA-CS scripts
(`rubric_eval.py`, `scholarqacs_rubric.py`, `convert_answer_scholar_cs.py`,
`parse_annotations.py`). They are not here: this harness never invokes them, and
the CS split is not one of the paper's rows.
